<file path="0E64.md">
A script in subindex 13, believed to have something to do with displaying papers with aspect < 2. (papers with aspect >= 2, but not 0xff, are handled by 0E65) It is called from 1086.Use with the parameters A2=0x21, A3=0x03, A4=0x26, A5=0x2C, A6=0x000000B6, A7=0x000000B8 

It uses gui_create with parameters (prop, A3=0x11, A4=0x27, A5=0x34, A6=0x000000B6, A7=0x000000B8) 

What I assume is the text widget (theText) has one of its attributes (0x41) set to A2. It seems to affect the typeface. 

   * 0x21 - regular black font. 0x00 regular white font. 0x23 bold black font. 


```
function (theObject,messageText,A2,A3,A4,A5,A6,A7) (theWindow, theText)
  ifn 
    opDB
      arg thePaper
    end
  then L000E

  return
    byte 0
  end
 
  L000E:
  set theWindow
    gui_create 
      arg thePaper
      arg A3
      arg A4
      arg A5
      arg A6
      arg A7
    end
  end

  set theText  ; Scroll text widget?
    gui_0x06
      local theWindow
      arg messageText
      byte 0
      byte 0
      arg A6
      arg A7
    end
  end

  setattr 0x41 of
    local theText
  to
    arg A2
  end

  return
    byte 0
  end
```
