<file path="dsencoder.py.md">
A simple program for writing [Delver Sprite Graphics](Delver-Sprite-Graphics). It currently doesn't do any compression, so the resulting graphics are much bigger than they should be. This is really just a novelty, but I do intend to make it use the run-length encoding operations at some point (which will result in very substantial savings.) 

Demonstration: Meleager gets some new threads from a friend. Too bad the friend was Magpie. (Note that this isn't just a recolor, the sprite also has Meleager's face.) 

![](dsencoder.py/mel1.png) 
